; Dual-zone extruder PID (Indy tool 0: H1 band + H2 nozzle).
; Strategy from https://forum.duet3d.com/topic/26910/strategy-for-pid-tuning-multiple-heat-zones/
;
; Run macros in order from COLD (all heaters off, ~25°C):
;   1) Tune H1 band alone
;   2) Tune H2 nozzle with H1 held hot (simulates band preheat)
;   3) Tune tool T0 with H2 held hot (simulates both zones in use)
;
; After each M303, copy the reported M307 line into config.g (or run config-sync).
; Repeat 2–3 until M307 values stabilise.
;
; G10 P0 Saaa:bbb  →  H1 (band) active : H2 (nozzle) active
;
; Clear a heater fault: M562 H2  (or DWC heater fault reset)

echo "=== Dual-zone heater PID ==="
echo "H1 = Bandheater (barrel)   H2 = Nozzle"
echo "1) Tune H1 band alone"
echo "2) Tune H2 nozzle with H1 hot"
echo "3) Tune tool with H2 hot"
echo "Start cold. Copy M307 lines from Console into config.g."
M291 P"See Console. Run macros 1→2→3 from cold. H1=band H2=nozzle." R"Dual-zone PID tune" S1
